Example of Request from Client─►API

/payments

``` 
POST /payments
{
    "correlationId": "4a7901b8-7d26-4d9d-aa19-4dc1c7cf60b3",
    "amount": 19.90
}

HTTP 2XX
Anything
```

Where `correlationId` is a unique UUID and `amount` is a required decimal value (fuck).



/payments-summary

```
GET /payments-summary?from=2020-07-10T12:34:56.000Z&to=2020-07-10T12:35:56.000Z

HTTP 200 - Ok
{
    "default" : {
        "totalRequests": 43236,
        "totalAmount": 415542345.98
    },
    "fallback" : {
        "totalRequests": 423545,
        "totalAmount": 329347.34
    }
}
```
from and to are ISO timestamps (3 hours ahead from Brasil)
both optional


this fields need to be int and decimal

IMPORTANT: The payment services also have a payments-summary endpoint
During the test, the API and the services will be called, and the responses must be an exact match or else it will punish you for inconsistency



















